                   ABOUT ME — Justin Ridings
================================================================

Engineer at Microsoft. US Army Veteran. Microsoft MSSA Graduate.

I work on Windows. Specifically, I make sure that when your machine
falls over you eventually get a fix from the team that owns the
component that fell over.

Things I've helped ship / build:

  > CTRL+SHIFT+WIN+B  — the black-screen recovery key combination
                        that resets your graphics stack on Windows.

  > !analyze SDK      — published on NuGet under @@BangAnalyze.
                        Tools for the WinDbg automation crowd.

  > SymProxyCloud     — open source on github.com/microsoft.
                        A modern, scalable Microsoft Symbol Server
                        proxy.

  > This site         — Blazor WebAssembly + .NET 10 + MudBlazor +
                        an unhealthy amount of fake XP CSS.

----------------------------------------------------------------

Click around. Most things work. Some things don't. That's
realistic for a Windows install.

Try opening:
  - PE Inspector.exe   (drop a .dll, parse it in your browser)
  - Pong.exe           (yes, really)
  - Internet Explorer  (don't worry, it opens in Edge)
  - Recycle Bin        (find out what got cut)

Press Ctrl+Alt+Del for a faithful tribute.

